        "id": "kestrel-overnight",
        "heading": "One night on battery: raccoon, low battery, solar, package",
        "text": [
          "Source: Kestrel Porch Cam HLD (input/hld.md, reviewed design, Kestrel Home platform team), operator answers, the approved Backstage catalog snapshot and reviewed code locations. For camera-platform and device-state engineers: which service acts at each moment, how the app's device page lags the camera's real battery, and how a Wi-Fi outage delays the package push.",
          "Operator times: start 10:30 PM, raccoon 1:10 AM, low-battery heartbeat 4:00 AM, sunrise 6:50 AM, courier 8:05 AM. Other minutes (7:00 AM charging heartbeat, 8:03 Wi-Fi drop, retries, 8:06 open, 8:16 late push) and the app values from heartbeats not shown are illustrative. Solar charge is shown as +3.5 %/h net (the HLD says 3–4 %/h).",
          "The given times and the HLD's ~1 %/h drain disagree: from 25% at 10:30 PM, 1 %/h plus the raccoon clip would reach 20% around 2:30 AM, not 4:00 AM. The battery is therefore held at 25% until the 4:00 AM report instead of inventing an in-between rate.",
          "device-shadow's offline rule (two missed heartbeats, 60 min) is linked on its node but never fires: the outage lasts about 12 minutes and misses no heartbeat."
        ],
